# A whitelist: the build context is exactly what the Dockerfile COPYs, and nothing else.
#
# This directory also holds the live database (data/, with its -wal/-shm sidecars and the
# set-aside copies db-layout.sh leaves there), the scheduler's job store
# (scheduler-data/), yfinance's cache, .env with every secret, local portfolio.db
# snapshots under any name, tests/ and venv/. A list of exclusions is always one name
# behind (.gitignore's history says so), and a future `COPY . .` would bake whatever it
# missed into the image. Everything is excluded first; a new COPY source needs its own
# `!` line, and CI's `image` job fails the build until it has one.
# tests/test_db_directory_mount.py pins this list against the Dockerfile's COPY lines.
*
!requirements.lock
!app/
!alembic/
!alembic.ini

# Inside the whitelisted trees: bytecode, and any database copy someone drops there.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.db
**/*.db.*
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite*
